<title>UK: Pechiney has no plans to restart idled capacity.</title>
<headline>Pechiney has no plans to restart idled capacity.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>French aluminium producer Pechiney at present has no plans to restart the 121,000 tonnes of aluminium production capacity that it has idled, Bernard Legrand, a senior executive, said.</p>
<p>Legrand said at a presentation to the Association of Mining Analysts that there were in total 980,000 tonnes of aluminium capacity idled worldwide. But with the market likely to be in balance in 1997 there was no need for this to be brought back this year.</p>
</text>
